  "title": "CMake: Require 3.20 for cmake_path",
  "description": "Commit 9d8da5d95aab52da50c789d60a253ace17c43be8 uses cmake_path,\nwhich was added in CMake 3.20. Make the requirement explicit instead\nof failing in the middle of the script on older versions.\n\nAmong popular Linux distributions, the biggest impact is to Ubuntu\n20.04 focal, which already requires unofficial packages to get a\nsupported Qt version and ends standard support in May 2025, and to\nDebian Bullseye (current oldstable), where the CMake from backports\nwill be needed. Note that while OSS-Fuzz bases its containers on\nUbuntu 20.04 for now, a more recent CMake (currently 3.29.2) is\ninstalled and used.\n\nRHEL 8 and SLES 15 have had CMake 3.20 for several point releases\n(8.5 and 15SP4), so it should not be a problem on updated systems.",
